 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“In the first place, Every general act of the Union must necessarily bear unequally hard on some particular member or members of it. Secondly the partiality of the members to their own interests and rights, a partiality which will be fostered by the Courtiers of popularity, will naturally exaggerate the inequality where it exists, and even suspect it where it has no existence. Thirdly a distrust of the voluntary compliance of each other may prevent the compliance of any, although it should be the latent disposition of all. Here are causes &amp; pretexts which will never fail to render federal measures abortive. If the laws of the States, were merely recommendatory to their citizens, or if they were to be rejudged by County authorities, what security, what probability would exist, that they would be carried into execution? Is the security or probability greater in favor of the acts of Congs. which depending for their execution on the will of the state legislatures, wch. are tho’ nominally authoritative, in fact recommendatory only.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">James Madison, <i>Vices of the Political System of the United States</i>, April 1787</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614989,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "According to James Madison, which of the following statements was not a problem with the government under the Articles of Confederation?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167928,
     "content_html": "There was no mechanism to hold states accountable to enforce federal laws through sanctions or a federal judiciary."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167927,
     "content_html": "Each state was unlikely to voluntarily cooperate with federal laws, because they suspected that other states were not held to compliance."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167929,
     "content_html": "Separation of powers caused the federal legislature to become tyrannical."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167926,
     "content_html": "Congress depended on the will of the state legislatures to enforce compliance with federal laws."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614990,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following characteristic of the 1787 Constitution directly addressed the issues Madison outlined in the excerpt provided?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167932,
     "content_html": "The “three-fifths” compromise, which meant that five slaves would count as three freemen for purposes of representation"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167933,
     "content_html": "Subordination of the laws of the states to those passed by a federal legislature, to be enforced by an executive office"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167931,
     "content_html": "The bicameral legislature, featuring representation based on both population and equal representation"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167930,
     "content_html": "The absence of a federal bill of rights, because many states had their own"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  }
